# Cleophis-owned R8/ProGuard rules. Hand-written — unlike proguard-tauri.pro and
# generated/proguard-wry.pro, which are autogenerated and must not be edited.
# Picked up automatically: the release buildType globs `**/*.pro` under app/.

# The JNI bridge's Kotlin end (src-tauri/src/android_bridge.rs calls it).
#
# This rule is load-bearing and its absence would ONLY show up in a release
# build. R8 shrinks on reachability from Java/Kotlin, and NativeBridge's sole
# caller is Rust across a JNI boundary, which R8 cannot see. So from R8's point
# of view `describeDevice` is dead code.
#
# The existing wry rule (`-keep class com.cleophis.app.* { native <methods>; }`)
# is NOT sufficient: it matches this class and so preserves the class NAME, but
# its member spec keeps only `native` methods. `describeDevice` is a plain
# static, has no Java caller, and would be removed — leaving a class that exists
# with the method missing, i.e. NoSuchMethodError at the call, not
# ClassNotFoundException. That is a worse symptom, because it points at the
# signature rather than at minification.
#
# Debug builds set isMinifyEnabled=false, so the on-device smoke test proves the
# bridge works and says NOTHING about whether it survives release. The two
# configurations diverge exactly here. Flagged for the Phase 5.2 release-config
# audit to confirm on a real release artifact, alongside debuggable=false,
# usesCleartextTraffic and the abiFilters check.
-keep class com.cleophis.app.NativeBridge { *; }

# Phase 3.2's AndroidKeyStore SecureStore — the second Kotlin entry point
# reached only from Rust, and the first one whose loss would be a SECURITY
# failure rather than a diagnostic one.
#
# Same reasoning as NativeBridge above, with a sharper consequence: if R8
# strips blobDir/encrypt/decrypt, the release build cannot read any stored
# credential, so every launch signs the user out — which looks exactly like a
# keystore or migration problem and nothing like minification. The debug
# checkpoint (sign in -> force-stop -> still signed in) passes green while the
# shipped build fails, because isMinifyEnabled is false for debug and true for
# release.
-keep class com.cleophis.app.SecureStore { *; }
